From 7a27594775f373d1195fd43111cda935eb6c0ae6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Parimalarengan Gururajan <gururaja@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 20:36:25 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] patch 3: 1905-layer security transport support

Add 1905 CMDU encryption/decryption/MIC support in the transport process
and the broker-side API to install the resulting keys:

- 1905_security_manager.{h,cpp} (new): encrypts/decrypts/MICs 1905 CMDUs
  using tlvEncryptedPayload/tlvMic, initialized with the AL MAC.
- dpp_crypto_helper.{h,cpp} (new, transport-local): OpenSSL EVP helper
  used by the security manager.
- ieee1905_transport.h/.cpp: owns m_security_manager; adds
  handle_security_key_install_message() and the SecurityKeyInstallMessage
  transport message type/factory case.
- broker_client.h/broker_client_impl.{h,cpp}: new
  BrokerClient::install_security_key() API used after a successful DPP
  4-way handshake to push TK/GTK into the transport process.
- message_parser_stream_impl.cpp: raises the broker's max payload size to
  16KB to accommodate large DPP BSS Config Response CMDUs.

Signed-off-by: Parimalarengan Gururajan <gururaja@qti.qualcomm.com>
